ve2`\n\nand the later:\n\n`ecai Phase 1 → Phase 2 → Phase 3`\n\nBoth are legitimate work, but the repository does not clearly state whether the wave lineage is:\n\n- prerequisite,\n- predecessor,\n- parallel scaffold,\n- or superseded substrate.\n\nLuce did **not** invent an answer, which is exactly right. fileciteturn0file0L83-L84\n\n---\n\n# Where I put us now\n\nI would freeze the operating statement as:\n\n> **EC8 AI Convergence is verified through its deterministic substrate and runtime foundation at Phase 3. The intelligence/convergence pipeline remains deliberately unimplemented under a Don/Coda Phase-4 hold. Methodology v0.3.2 is the latest sealed candidate but is not yet promoted to canon.**\n\nThat is the clean ground truth.\n\nAnd Luce respected the most important boundary: **Quant was not entered or used in the recon.** fileciteturn0file0L14-L18\n\n## What I would do next\n\nI would **not release Phase 4 yet**.\n\nFirst we do a short **Coda reconciliation pass**, not a build pass:\n\n1. Close the v0.3.2 governance holds and determine whether it becomes canon.\n2. Resolve the **five-persona methodology vs four-role runtime** conflict.\n3. Resolve the **Mantle vs classic Converse** runtime authority conflict using our now-current Bedrock evidence.\n4. Clarify whether `wave0–2` is predecessor/supporting substrate or a parallel active lineage.\n5. Then return to Don with a **Phase 4 release package**, not a pile of unresolved documents.\n\nThat matches Luce's own routing: canon/holds first, Phase-4 authority second, runtime/persona conflicts before Phase 4.1 construction. fileciteturn0file0L114-L124\n\n**So we're in a much better place than it looked from Explorer.** The estate isn't chaos; it's basically **one unfinished methodology promotion + two architectural conflicts sitting immediately in front of a deliberate Phase-4 gate.**"]}, "create_time": 1790219386.687768, "end_turn": true, "id": "4f1b3803-22b6-47b5-a4c7-321ab1777683", "metadata": {